MID_BD11_00_m01: <TH>
MID_BD11_00_m01_001: Be careful, Cai! She's really mad!
MID_BD11_00_m02: <TH>
MID_BD11_00_m02_001: Cai! I think this is your chance!
MID_BD11_00_m02_002: I'm going for it! I'll get 'em this time.
MID_SC11_01_m01: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_m01_001: Hey! Gimme back my mom's necklace!
MID_SC11_01_m01_002: Damn it. Couldn't shake him. Persistent brat!
MID_SC11_01_m10: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_m01_003: Cai! What's going on? Who're the scary guys?
MID_SC11_01_m01_004: Peter! Tialla! What are you two doing here?
MID_SC11_01_m02: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_m02_001: I-I'm scared, but I'll do my best for my friends!
MID_SC11_01_m03: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_m03_001: Peter, what're you doing out here?
MID_SC11_01_m03_002: I saw you running with a wild look on your face, so I\nchased after you.
MID_SC11_01_m03_003: I'm glad you're here. I could use a little help.
MID_SC11_01_m04: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_m04_001: All that magic I studied in Grandpa's books is about\nto come in real handy.
MID_SC11_01_m05: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_m05_001: Cai! Happy birthday!
MID_SC11_01_m05_002: Thanks, Tialla. But I don't have time for that.
MID_SC11_01_m05_003: They stole my mom's heirloom necklace!
MID_SC11_01_m05_004: What?! We can't let that stand! We're getting it back!
MID_SC11_01_m06: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_m06_001: Wh-who the heck are these guys?
MID_SC11_01_m07: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_m07_001: My mom's necklace embedded itself in my hand!\nWhat's happening to me?
MID_SC11_01_m07_002: Ugh! It's hot! It's burning!
MID_SC11_01_m11: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_m07_003: This is bad. Looks like we've got our hands\nfull again!
MID_SC11_01_m07_004: Urrrgh... Uwaaargh!
MID_SC11_01_m12: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_m07_005: Huh? Wh-what?! Hot hot hot hot!
MID_SC11_01_m07_006: What... Was that, magic? Cai, was that you?
MID_SC11_01_m07_007: It's like my mom's necklace is helping us.
MID_SC11_01_m08: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_m08_001: Cai! Are you sure you're OK?
MID_SC11_01_m08_002: Yeah. I'm OK. Mostly. I think.
MID_SC11_01_m09: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_m09_001: Looks like we did it...somehow.
MID_SC11_01_e04: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_e04_001: We'll take care of these guys! You go make sure the\nboss gets that necklace!
MID_SC11_01_e05: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_e05_001: Guess I'd best lay low here for now. Where's\nthe boss, anyway?
MID_SC11_01_e08: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_e08_001: Am I too late? Damn. How dare they do this to my\nloyal henchmen!
MID_SC11_01_e14: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_e14_001: You brat! I'll kill you!
MID_SC11_01_e15: <TH>
MID_SC11_01_e15_001: N-nah! I'm not going down like this! Time to retreat!
MID_BD11_02_m01: <TH>
MID_BD11_02_m01_001: It's that crew from the village! Good. We'll kill 'em\nright here.
MID_BD11_02_m01_002: I don't think those guys are looking for a\nfriendly chat.
MID_BD11_02_m04: <TH>
MID_BD11_02_m01_003: I guess we'll hit these knuckleheads so hard they'll\nforget what they wanted with us in the first place.
MID_BD11_02_m05: <TH>
MID_BD11_02_m01_004: It figures. You have this way of getting us deeper into\ntrouble whenever you try to take charge.
MID_BD11_02_m02: <TH>
MID_BD11_02_m02_001: Castor, is it really true what my grandpa said?\nWere you a vulkan?
MID_BD11_02_m02_002: Well, yes, but... These days I'm just a guy who\ngot axed.
MID_BD11_02_m06: <TH>
MID_BD11_02_m02_003: That's ancient history though. Let's just deal with\nthese idiots, OK?
MID_BD11_02_m03: <TH>
MID_BD11_02_m03_001: Damn it. So this is where it ends...
MID_BD11_02_m03_002: I think that wraps things up. Let's get going.
MID_SC11_03_m01: <TH>
MID_SC11_03_m01_001: Listen up! Take everything from those passengers.\nGet anything valuable.
MID_SC11_03_e01: <TH>
MID_SC11_03_e01_002: {SetColor=Gold}Guard the carriage!{SetColor=Default} Don't let the thieves destroy it!
MID_SC11_03_e02: <TH>
MID_SC11_03_e02_001: Damn... They destroyed the carriage!
MID_SC11_03_e03: <TH>
MID_SC11_03_e03_001: Good work. Now all we have to do is sit back and\nrelax until we're in Dagsion.
MID_SC11_03_e03_002: I hope that's the last time anything like that happens.
MID_SC11_04_m01: <TH>
MID_SC11_04_m01_001: Bwahahahaha! You little twerps really think you can\ntake me out? Sure, give it a try!
MID_SC11_04_m02: <TH>
MID_SC11_04_m02_001: Your moves... Where did you learn to do that?
MID_SC11_04_m02_002: My pop taught me. He trained me every day since I\nwas little.
MID_SC11_04_m02_003: {SetColor=Gray}Those are the movements of a well-trained vulkan\nfighter...a very talented one at that.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SC11_04_m02_004: {SetColor=Gray}Who is this kid? And who is his father?{SetColor=Default}
MID_SC11_04_m03: <TH>
MID_SC11_04_m03_001: Bwahaha! What's wrong? Come get me!
MID_SC11_04_m04: <TH>
MID_SC11_04_m04_001: Don't overdo it! If you're hurt, give me a shout, and\nI'll heal you!
MID_SC11_04_m05: <TH>
MID_SC11_04_m05_001: We did it!
MID_SC11_04_e01: <TH>
MID_SC11_04_e01_001: *yawn* So boring. I should move.
MID_SC11_05_m01: <TH>
MID_SC11_05_m01_001: Drew a top-notch opponent. Just my luck.
MID_SC11_05_m01_002: Heh, better focus on the weaklings to score some\npoints and qualify.
MID_SC11_05_m01_003: Listen up! Leave the Saraminian queen alone.\nPick off the weaklings instead.
MID_SC11_05_m01_004: Oh! Everyone seems to be looking my way\nquite intently!
MID_SC11_05_m01_005: Ugh. I feel like they're looking at me too.
MID_SC11_05_m02: <TH>
MID_SC11_05_m02_001: Alright! That's one for me.
MID_SC11_05_m02_002: {SetColor=Gray}The boy fights suspiciously well for his years.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SC11_05_m03: <TH>
MID_SC11_05_m03_001: Was that your best? From mediocrity you came, and\nto mediocrity you are forever resigned.
MID_SC11_05_m04: <TH>
MID_SC11_05_m04_001: Oh, I do hope that my opponent will be alright...
MID_SC11_05_m04_002: Focus, cat priest. Our trial is not yet over.
MID_SC11_05_m05: <TH>
MID_SC11_05_m05_001: Are you alright, boy? Recklessness is a sure way to\nturn triumph into defeat.
MID_SC11_05_m05_002: What, this? It's nothing, Sis. You just take care\nof yourself!
MID_SC11_05_m06: <TH>
MID_SC11_05_m06_001: You lot, move! Smash 'em to bits, starting with the\nweak ones.
MID_SC11_05_m06_002: Wretches and reprobates, all of them. They live\ndown to my estimation in every way.
MID_SC11_05_m07: <TH>
MID_SC11_05_m07_001: You there, boy! Do not let your reach exceed\nyour grasp.
MID_SC11_05_m07_002: We're fine, Sis! Look after yourselves too!
MID_SC11_05_m07_003: "Sis"? Hmph. You are far too familiar with me.
MID_SC11_05_m08: <TH>
MID_SC11_05_m08_001: This is our first big brawl, but we'll be fine if we just\ndo what we usually do.
MID_SC11_05_m09: <TH>
MID_SC11_05_m09_001: I'll do my best to use a light touch. I honestly\ndon't want to see you get hurt.
MID_SC11_05_m10: <TH>
MID_SC11_05_m10_001: I shall show you how we deal with blackguards of\nyour ilk in Saramis.
MID_SC11_05_m11: <TH>
MID_SC11_05_m11_001: A thief's gotta do what a thief's gotta do. Let the\ncrowd see that I got guts!
MID_SC11_05_m12: <TH>
MID_SC11_05_m12_001: Damn it, I can't be done! This can't be the end for\nme, can it?!
MID_SC11_05_e01: <TH>
MID_SC11_05_e01_001: Zarcone seems unremarkable enough, but that\nexterior masks a formidable foe.
MID_SC11_05_e01_002: He may be one of those skilled fighters who {SetColor=Gold}rises\nagain after an initial defeat{SetColor=Default}. Be wary.
MID_SC11_05_e02: <TH>
MID_SC11_05_e02_001: You ready? Anyone gets near me, take 'em down!\nGang up and do it!
MID_SC11_06_m01: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m02_001: Ha! Ahahaha! I got this in the bag! These guys are\nnothing but a bunch of amateurs!
MID_SC11_06_m02_002: They can work together all they want, but they'll\nnever match the teamwork of my crew.
MID_SC11_06_m01_001: Right! Time to show these inexperienced grunts\nwhat war is all about!
MID_SC11_06_m05: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m05_001: Armored units! Get out front, and stop the enemies\nin their tracks!
MID_SC11_06_m06: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m06_001: This is our chance! Chariots! Move in!\nDisrupt 'em!
MID_SC11_06_m08: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m08_001: Hahaha! This match is mine!
MID_SC11_06_m09: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m09_001: Hahaha! We blew 'em outta the water! Doesn't get\nany better than this!
MID_SC11_06_m10: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m10_001: If we use these, maybe we can severely limit the\nmobility of the enemy's chariots.
MID_SC11_06_m21: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m10_002: Everyone! {SetColor=Gold}Knock down the big pillars!{SetColor=Default}
MID_SC11_06_m11: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m11_001: {SetColor=Gold}Don't stand in front{SetColor=Default} of a chariot! Look where it's\ngoing, and {SetColor=Gold}get to the side or go behind it{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SC11_06_m11_003: What?! How does that little brat know how to\nhandle chariots?!
MID_SC11_06_m12: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m12_001: {SetColor=Gold}Magic users{SetColor=Default}, target the {SetColor=Gold}armored infantry first{SetColor=Default}, and\nshut them down!
MID_SC11_06_m13: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m13_001: Wh-why you little... How dare you get in the way of\nmy glory!
MID_SC11_06_m14: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m14_001: You're a surprisingly lively old geezer, a bigger\nloudmouth than me!
MID_SC11_06_m15: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m15_001: I got to know quite a few generals in my line of work,\nbut I never heard of you.
MID_SC11_06_m15_002: Wha... What are you talking about?! You won't make\na fool outta me!
MID_SC11_06_m16: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m16_001: I'll pin you to my chest like another war medal!
MID_SC11_06_m17: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m17_001: After what happened, I thought a little about your\ntrue identity. I have a hypothesis.
MID_SC11_06_m17_002: Perhaps you and your kin are...sailors? Or possibly\nthe descendants of sailors?
MID_SC11_06_m17_003: Silence! I'll hear nothing from an affiliate of Vritra!
MID_SC11_06_m18: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m18_001: Fabio, you use some strange magic. I don't think I've\never seen it before.
MID_SC11_06_m18_002: Hmm... Though you are curious, it would be better\nthat you focus on the task at hand.
MID_SC11_06_m19: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m19_001: Well done.
MID_SC11_06_m20: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_m20_001: Ugh, how could I lose? How could a little brat like\nthat be so good at this?
MID_SC11_06_m20_002: She was like a seasoned tactician! But at her age?\nIt's ridiculous!
MID_SC11_06_m20_003: Impossible... My dreams can't be crushed into dust...\nNot here... Not like this...
MID_SC11_06_e01: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_e01_001: Chariot corps! Start your charge at the enemy!
MID_SC11_06_e10: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_e10_001: What would my grandpa do at a time like this?\nThink, Tialla...
MID_SC11_06_e04: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_e04_001: Infantry, open the chests! Grab whatever's in them!
MID_SC11_06_e05: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_e05_001: I think the {SetColor=Gold}chests{SetColor=Default} contain weapons. Let's {SetColor=Gold}get what's\nin them before the enemy{SetColor=Default} does. Hmm, if we can...
MID_SC11_06_e06: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_e06_001: Haha! Good, give it to me! I don't want any of those\nguys to get their hands on it!
MID_SC11_06_e07: <TH>
MID_SC11_06_e07_001: Dignity he may lack, but he is a hardened veteran.
MID_SC11_06_e07_002: We must take care. Among their ranks are {SetColor=Gold}those who\nwill rise again to fight even after defeat{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC11_07_m01: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_m01_001: Even among the fearsome forest peoples, the\nHar Hali are revered for their skills in warfare.
MID_SC11_07_m01_002: Ultand and I are here to protect you, but don't drop\nyour guard for a moment, Cai!
MID_SC11_07_m01_003: No need to tell me that, Centurio!
MID_SC11_07_m03: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_m03_001: Trespassers on these sacred Har Hali grounds,\nwhoever you are, you will pay!
MID_SC11_07_m04: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_m04_001: That... That's the power of the demon god!
MID_SC11_07_m04_002: Yes! You wield the demon god's might! Just like\nBahr Vahn!
MID_SC11_07_m04_003: Demon god? Do they mean Balor?
MID_SC11_07_e01: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_e01_001: Spellsong chanters, begin your recitations! Sing the\nsong of the Har Hali!
MID_SC11_07_e02: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_e02_001: We sing for our people!
MID_SC11_07_e03: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_e03_001: The fog is so thick... The enemy could be anywhere.
MID_SC11_07_e03_002: We must take care. This situation is a poor one.
MID_SC11_07_e05: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_e05_001: <DLG>The singer performed a Defense Chant.\nThe Har Hali warriors have increased defense.
MID_SC11_07_e06: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_e06_001: <DLG>The singer performed a Prayer Chant.\nThe Har Hali warriors have increased resistance.
MID_SC11_07_e07: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_e07_001: <DLG>The singer performed a Hunting Chant.\nThe Har Hali warriors have increased attack.
MID_SC11_07_e08: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_e08_001: Yes... I feel the power filling me! Through my every\nmuscle and limb!
MID_SC11_07_e08_002: Is that...spellsong?! This is a bad sign. Their strength\nis increasing!
MID_SC11_07_e10: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_e10_001: The time has come for my song. Hear me!
MID_SC11_07_e11: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_e11_001: And now it is my turn to sing from the soul.
MID_SC11_07_e12: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_e12_001: Warriors, form on me! Then crash upon our enemy\nlike an annihilating wave!
MID_SC11_07_e12_002: D-did you hear that? He's calling for even more of his\nfriends to attack us!
MID_SC11_07_e12_003: We could have a dozen Centurios with us and this\nwould still be a dangerous situation.
MID_SC11_07_e12_004: We've got to stop the singing. Let's {SetColor=Gold}target the\ndiviners{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SC11_07_e15: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_e15_001: My chief, we have come as you asked. It won't be\nlong before our comrades join us.
MID_SC11_07_e16: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_e16_001: Is everyone here? Then follow me! Death to those\nwho trespass on this land!
MID_SC11_07_e17: <TH>
MID_SC11_07_e17_001: The {SetColor=Gold}spellsong singers{SetColor=Default} are strengthening the enemy.\n{SetColor=Gold}Defeat them quickly!{SetColor=Default}
MID_BD11_08_m01: <TH>
MID_BD11_08_m01_001: This risen dead... It's not like the others.\nIt's much stronger.
MID_BD11_08_m01_002: Cai, can we do this? It looks so powerful.
MID_BD11_08_m02: <TH>
MID_BD11_08_m02_001: Kill! Destroy everything!
MID_BD11_08_m06: <TH>
MID_BD11_08_m02_002: Is that voice... Is it from the dead? Or...is it coming\nfrom inside me?
MID_BD11_08_m02_003: It's echoing inside my head... What is it?
MID_BD11_08_m03: <TH>
MID_BD11_08_m03_001: I see you're in quite a bind. Fear not. We're here.
MID_BD11_08_m03_002: You're the one I met in Ribeira... The herald...\nHerald...of the Pale Raven?
MID_BD11_08_m04: <TH>
MID_BD11_08_m04_001: The spear you wield... Is that some kind of Arc?
MID_BD11_08_m04_002: Or...perhaps it's something more powerful. I feel as\nthough I've seen it somewhere else.
MID_BD11_08_m04_003: But I've never heard of a being like you in the\ntemples. Who are you?
MID_BD11_08_m05: <TH>
MID_BD11_08_m05_001: This brute is not so easy to dispose of, is he? 'Tis\nwhat comes of challenging Balor in his lair.
MID_BD11_08_m05_002: Let us finish things here. The rest of you should\nmake haste to leave.
MID_BD11_08_m05_003: Many thanks for your assistance. I'll escort the\nchildren to safety.
MID_BD11_08_m05_004: Can one fighter handle this?
MID_BD11_08_m07: <TH>
MID_BD11_08_m05_005: I don't know who that is, but a warrior wielding a\nweapon similar to a Supreme Arc...
MID_BD11_08_m05_006: That's no ordinary fighter. Let's leave it to them\nand escape.
MID_BD11_08_m05_007: Fear not. As long as you have the Divine Sand, I'll be\nby your side.
MID_BD11_08_m05_008: Y-yeah, I got it. Please take care of yourself!
MID_BD11_08_m05_009: Cai, you and I will meet again someday.
MID_BD11_08_m08: <TH>
MID_BD11_08_m05_010: Huh? That voice... Was it the Herald of the\nPale Raven?
MID_SC11_09_m01: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_m01_001: Grrrrrr... Kill, kill, KIIILLLL!
MID_SC11_09_m01_002: Hey, is she alright? Your friend there isn't looking\nso great.
MID_SC11_09_m01_003: ...
MID_SC11_09_m03: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_m03_001: So you have that power too... Yes, you do...
MID_SC11_09_m03_002: No matter... I'll kill you and claim that power...\nfor myself.
MID_SC11_09_m03_003: Give it to me! I'll gather them all! I'll be a goddess!
MID_SC11_09_m03_004: A goddess, huh? Not afraid to aim high, are you?
MID_SC11_09_m05: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_m05_001: And now...out comes the flamma. Is she finally\nhitting her wall?
MID_SC11_09_m02_001: I can hear it... The voice...
MID_SC11_09_m02_002: What's this "voice" you keep talking about?
MID_SC11_09_m02_003: Destroy... Destroy... All of it!
MID_SC11_09_m02_004: Huh? That voice... Is it the same as before?
MID_SC11_09_m02_005: Hm.
MID_SC11_09_m04_001: Now's not the time to pull punches. I've got to take\nthis seriously.
MID_SC11_09_m06: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_m06_001: She's using a magic item to summon the risen dead?
MID_SC11_09_m06_002: Wait...does Obsidian draw its power from the same\nsource? It can't be...
MID_SC11_09_m07: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_m07_001: Hey, I haven't given up, you know. On getting you\nto sell me that bow, I mean.
MID_SC11_09_m07_002: ...
MID_SC11_09_m07_003: Right. Well, you just think it over. We can discuss\nfurther after I win.
MID_SC11_09_m08: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_m08_001: Miss, you're not looking so good. Are you OK?
MID_SC11_09_m08_002: ...
MID_SC11_09_m09: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_m09_001: Will you just...die?
MID_SC11_09_m10: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_m10_001: No, defeat isn't an option for me either.
MID_SC11_09_m11: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_m11_001: I really shouldn't be playing so carelessly, but I don't\nhave a choice, now do I?
MID_SC11_09_m12: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_m12_001: I think we can make it through with help like this.
MID_SC11_09_m12_002: Less talk, more focus, please. You've gotta get\nmoving and take them down!
MID_SC11_09_m12_003: In the meantime, I'll do my best to keep this up.
MID_SC11_09_m12_004: But this is draining. I can't go on forever, OK?
MID_SC11_09_m13: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_m13_001: String of Earth, Obsidian... Rose of Caelus, you make\nit sing beautifully, as ever.
MID_SC11_09_m13_002: Yes, strum your soul for me. Play the melody of hate\nthat wells up from the depths of your heart.
MID_SC11_09_m13_003: Such a lovely tune. Father would approve.
MID_SC11_09_m13_004: I must admit, it leaves me feeling a little jealous.
MID_SC11_09_m15: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_m15_001: Hmph, dealing with the undead is a notorious pain!\nHere! {SetColor=Gold}This sword{SetColor=Default} should keep things in our favor.
MID_SC11_09_m16: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_m16_001: {SetColor=Gold}Normal attacks won't do much against the undead.{SetColor=Default}\nBut that {SetColor=Gold}cleansing blade is different{SetColor=Default}. Use it well!
MID_SC11_09_e20: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_e20_001: What's this... I'm losing power...
MID_SC11_09_e20_002: Excellent! The wall has vanished, and the enemy is\nopen! Let's take her down.
MID_SC11_09_e07: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_e07_001: My {SetColor=Gold}Song of Abjuring {SetColor=Default}should be {SetColor=Gold}effective against the\nrisen dead {SetColor=Default}too. Might be worth a try.
MID_SC11_09_e08: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_e08_001: Is that a {SetColor=Gold}ballista{SetColor=Default}? So these guys prefer ranged attacks.
MID_SC11_09_e09: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_e09_001: Ughhh...
MID_SC11_09_e14: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_e14_001: The enemy has {SetColor=Gold}a lot of archers{SetColor=Default}. It might be safer for\nour flying units to dismount and{SetColor=Gold} fight on foot{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC11_09_e16: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_e16_001: <DLG>Inyoni will launch a long-range bow attack in the\nnext enemy phase.
MID_SC11_09_e17: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_e17_001: Huh?! Even if she does have Ugo's Bow, shooting at\nus from that far is insane.
MID_SC11_09_e18: <TH>
MID_SC11_09_e18_001: ...
MID_SC11_09_e18_002: {SetColor=Gold}That woman{SetColor=Default} is gonna be a real problem...
MID_SC11_09_e18_003: Seems she's got lots of tricks up her sleeve.\nWe should probably {SetColor=Gold}defeat her first{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC11_10_m01: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m01_001: I hate to tell you this, but I'm starting things off\nwith everything I've got. 
MID_SC11_10_m13: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m01_002: Don't do it, Leda! The power's too dangerous!
MID_SC11_10_m01_003: Leda, you hear it too, don't you? The voice? You\ncan't obey it!
MID_SC11_10_m01_004: If you can hear the voice, then why don't you follow\nyour own advice? Go on...withdraw!
MID_SC11_10_m14: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m01_005: You're acting like an idiot! Why don't you care\nabout yourself?
MID_SC11_10_m01_006: Why can't you see that you're surrounded by people\nwho deeply care about you?
MID_SC11_10_m01_007: They all love you, Leda! And this is how you\nrepay them?
MID_SC11_10_m01_008: That's none of your business! You better shut that\nloud mouth of yours before I shut it for you!
MID_SC11_10_m02: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m02_001: Rrr... Milady, please forgive me!
MID_SC11_10_m02_002: Buccar? What are you doing?!
MID_SC11_10_m15: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m02_003: What a mess! Have you lost your mind, Buccar?\nI'm sorry, but I won't go along with this.
MID_SC11_10_m16: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m02_004: I would give my own life if that's what it takes to\nstop you, milady.
MID_SC11_10_m02_005: I beg you to stop. This is not the way. Nothing but\nruin awaits you down this path.
MID_SC11_10_m02_006: I want only to save you from that. And if I fail, then\nI'll have failed to keep my promise to Lord Guillermo.
MID_SC11_10_m02_007: Even if you get your revenge, your heart will not\nknow peace! That much is clear to me!
MID_SC11_10_m02_008: If my life ends, it ends. But I want you to go on\nliving. I want you to find real happiness.
MID_SC11_10_m02_009: That was my promise to your father. And it's all\nI've ever wanted.
MID_SC11_10_m17: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m02_010: What? That's what this is about? That's why you're\nbetraying me?
MID_SC11_10_m02_011: This is...unforgivable! I will never, EVER, forgive you\nfor this, Buccar!
MID_SC11_10_m03: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m03_001: I will not lose! I will save my father!
MID_SC11_10_m03_002: Curse your reasons! Stand aside, Leda!
MID_SC11_10_m03_003: Shut up! Just because you're a stupid child doesn't\nmean you're the only one with something to lose!
MID_SC11_10_m04: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m04_001: I will show no mercy. I don't care who stands\nagainst me!
MID_SC11_10_m05: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m05_001: Bertrand is a good man. Why don't you at least talk\nto him?
MID_SC11_10_m05_002: You understand what I'm saying deep down, Leda.\nI know you do.
MID_SC11_10_m05_003: That's why Buccar wants to stop you!
MID_SC11_10_m06: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m06_001: Miss Leda, I am not an insensitive man. Understand,\nI have no desire to get in your way...
MID_SC11_10_m06_002: But I must make sure... Are you really and\ntruly alright?
MID_SC11_10_m18: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m06_003: So close... I can almost reach...his neck...
MID_SC11_10_m07: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m07_001: Leda, I want to stop you to save my father. It's true.
MID_SC11_10_m07_002: I also want to save Bertrand, but...
MID_SC11_10_m07_003: It's more than that, Leda. If you do what you're\ntrying to do, it won't bring happiness to anyone.
MID_SC11_10_m07_004: Your murderous rage won't give you satisfaction.
MID_SC11_10_m08: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m08_001: Buccar! You betrayed me. I will make sure you\npay for that!
MID_SC11_10_m08_002: Do as you will. Even if I pay for it with my life, I will\nstop you, milady.
MID_SC11_10_m09: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m09_001: I never thought you would betray her. For once, I am\ntoo shocked for words.
MID_SC11_10_m09_002: Think what you will. I can only follow my heart.
MID_SC11_10_m10: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m10_001: Buccar, I just can't bring myself to believe it. You, of\nall people, betraying Leilidahna...
MID_SC11_10_m10_002: Perhaps... Perhaps there's more to it than that.\nPerhaps this is the form your loyalty takes.
MID_SC11_10_m11: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m11_001: Buccar... I don't know what to do.
MID_SC11_10_m11_002: Don't worry. You do not need to take my side in this.\nThis is my burden.
MID_SC11_10_m12: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_m12_001: No... I lost? And to a...kid?!
MID_SC11_10_m12_002: It's not that you lost, Leda. It's more like I won.
MID_SC11_10_m12_003: Not quite... I'm going to make an exception and lend\nmy support.
MID_SC11_10_m19: <TH>
MID_SC12_09_m03_001: Mu! What are you doing here? I told you to go back\nto your aunt!
MID_SC12_09_m03_002: Leave me alone, Mom. I can make my\nown decisions!
MID_SC12_09_m03_003: Mom? What are you doing here?!
MID_SC12_09_m03_004: Mu? I'm the one who should be saying that to you!\nWhat are you doing here?
MID_SC12_09_m03_005: When the battle is over, you'll tell me all about it.
MID_SC11_10_e03: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_e03_001: What is that?
MID_SC11_10_e04: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_e04_001: Those are {SetColor=Gold}explosives{SetColor=Default}! If you {SetColor=Gold}attack them{SetColor=Default}, it might\n{SetColor=Gold}defeat enemies caught in the blast{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SC11_10_e04_002: But the enemy certainly knows that as well. Don't get\ncaught too close to the explosives. Be careful!
MID_SC11_10_e08: <TH>
MID_SC11_10_e08_001: Waahhh! Look! That thing's moving!
MID_SC11_10_e08_002: Calm down, Peter! Its movements should be pretty\nstraightforward and easy to predict.
MID_SC11_10_e08_003: Position units to {SetColor=Gold}lure it into a fight{SetColor=Default} on our terms!
MID_BD11_10_m01: <TH>
MID_BD11_10_m01_001: That musician... Who is she? Isn't this in violation of\nthe rules?
MID_BD11_10_m01_002: Is it really so awful though? It's making the battle\nburn all the hotter, with so much more passion.
MID_BD11_10_m01_003: Ah... And doesn't it have a wonderful timbre?\nDon't you think so too, Babbu?
MID_BD11_10_m01_004: Er... Indeed. Well, we shall watch and see how all\nthis plays out.
MID_BD11_10_m02: <TH>
MID_BD11_10_m02_001: I've got your back! Cai, take care of that thing!
MID_BD11_10_m02_002: Thanks! I got it, Buccar!
MID_BD11_10_m03: <TH>
MID_BD11_10_m03_001: Looks like we cleared up the mess this time, huh?
MID_BD11_10_m03_002: Milady...
MID_BD11_10_e01: <TH>
MID_BD11_10_e01_001: The match is decided!
MID_BD11_10_e01_002: After a battle of extraordinary intensity, the\nwinner is...
MID_BD11_10_e02: <TH>
MID_BD11_10_e01_003: Ribeira Winds!
MID_BD11_10_e01_004: Everyone, let's hear a roaring cheer!
MID_SC11_11_m01: <TH>
MID_SC11_11_m01_001: Who are you people? How did you get here?
MID_SC11_11_m01_002: You must be Zenzele. Let Ultand go!
MID_SC11_11_m01_003: And you can set all your other victims free too!
MID_SC11_11_m01_004: This picture... This is my paradise. But it isn't\nfinished yet.
MID_SC11_11_m01_005: Like it or not, you're part of my family now too.
MID_SC11_11_m01_006: You want to make us a permanent part of your\npainting, you mean. No thanks. We're not interested.
MID_SC11_11_m01_007: Silence! In this place, I am the only god!
MID_SC11_11_m02: <TH>
MID_SC11_11_m02_001: My family portrait is far from complete. I must\nacquire more souls.
MID_SC11_11_m02_002: My family must grow. I must build my picture-\nperfect paradise!
MID_SC11_11_m03: <TH>
MID_SC11_11_m03_001: If only that woman hadn't tried to cast me aside...\nAlas, I had to turn her into paint.
MID_SC11_11_m03_002: With Bragi's Brush, I can truly capture my desires!
MID_SC11_11_m03_003: I will live forever with my family, inside this perfect\npicture of happiness.
MID_SC11_11_m03_004: After all, a family ought to sacrifice everything for\ntheir brilliant patriarch. It's only fair.
MID_SC11_11_m03_005: You know nothing about family. Ultand's family\nis going through some hard times...
MID_SC11_11_m03_006: And she's putting her heart and soul into doing\nall she can to bring them together again.
MID_SC11_11_m03_007: Still, she'd never do what you're doing. You care\nonly about yourself!
MID_SC11_11_m04: <TH>
MID_SC11_11_m04_001: Why... Why did you leave me, my bride?
MID_SC11_11_m04_002: I am not your bride! You can't choose that for me!
MID_SC11_11_m05: <TH>
MID_SC11_11_m05_001: Oh... I've never seen such a beautiful girl. I didn't\nrealize such beauty could exist.
MID_SC11_11_m05_002: You're a bride worthy of an artist. Come to me...
MID_SC11_11_m05_003: Silence! This paradise you've painted is not yours\nto inhabit.
MID_SC11_11_m05_004: You dare to sit where only the progenitor god can\nrightly sit! Your presence is sacrilege!
MID_SC11_11_m06: <TH>
MID_SC11_11_m06_001: This paradise is my world! It is my everything! I've\npoured my life into my creation!
MID_SC11_11_m06_002: Why must you trample it? Why would anyone want\nto destroy it?
MID_SC11_11_m06_003: Grrgh... Kill! Kill the defilers of paradise!\nKill them all!
MID_SC11_11_m07: <TH>
MID_SC11_11_m07_001: Ohhh... My paradise... My family's eternal dwelling...\nIt's collapsing...
MID_SC11_11_m07_002: The painting is crumbling! Cai, we must get out!
MID_SC11_11_e01: <TH>
MID_SC11_11_e01_001: I can't see anything in this fog, but they're out there.\nBe careful and {SetColor=Gold}watch for enemy movement{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC11_11_e02: <TH>
MID_SC11_11_e02_001: We're doing it! Press the attack!
MID_SC11_12_m01: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_m01_001: When we first met, I thought you to be little more\nthan a minor obstacle.
MID_SC11_12_m01_002: The time has come for me to defeat you and end\nour ill-fated entanglement.
MID_SC11_12_m02: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_m02_001: This is absurd. How is the queen of Saramis being\ndriven into a corner by mere children?
MID_SC11_12_m03: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_m03_001: I know you already know this, but I'm not planning\non losing this fight.
MID_SC11_12_m03_002: You stand before me undaunted? I see that the boy\nhas come into his own.
MID_SC11_12_m04: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_m04_001: I shall show no mercy to anyone who hopes to bar\nmy path with force.
MID_SC11_12_m04_002: Let the beating you are about to receive teach you\nhow Saramis deals with its foes!
MID_SC11_12_m05: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_m05_001: It cannot end this way...
MID_SC11_12_m05_002: I still have a duty to fulfill. The long-held dream of\nmy people will not be denied.
MID_SC11_12_m05_003: They cry out for Yu Phas to be honored once more!
MID_SC11_12_e01: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_e01_001: Archers! Thin their ranks with your arrows! The\nrest of you, weave into the gaps and break them all!
MID_SC11_12_e01_002: Armored ornius riders, hold your positions.\nDo not break formation until my command!
MID_SC11_12_e01_003: We're at a disadvantage on this terrain against ornius\nriders, but they're holding position for now.
MID_SC11_12_e04: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_e04_001: We can't do anything about Theodora herself until\nwe've gotten past the units protecting her.
MID_SC11_12_e05: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_e05_001: They make to challenge us, do they? Very well.\nArmored ornius riders, engage our foes!
MID_SC11_12_e06: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_e06_001: The time is now. Armored ornius riders, advance!
MID_SC11_12_e07: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_e07_001: Watch out for the ornius riders! They'll come flying\nover the walls any moment!
MID_SC11_12_e08: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_e08_001: Hm, so they broke through our siege. No farther!\nStop them in their tracks!
MID_SC11_12_e09: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_e09_001: The spectators just threw some things into the arena.\nMaybe they'll be useful for the fight?
MID_SC11_12_e09_002: Let's try to get to them before Theodora's units can!
MID_SC11_12_e10: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_e10_001: Guess I'd better make a show of trying for Her\nMajesty's sake.
MID_SC11_12_e11: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_e11_001: I stand before you as Lysander, son of Kleitos!\nLet our battle be fair and honorable!
MID_SC11_12_e12: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_e12_001: So long as I draw breath, I shall let none of you pass!
MID_SC11_12_e13: <TH>
MID_SC11_12_e13_001: Hate to break it to you, but there's no way you're\ngettin' past me!
MID_BD11_12_m01: <TH>
MID_BD11_12_m01_001: Kill... Destroy... All will burn...
MID_BD11_12_m01_002: What's going on? The queen of Saramis doesn't\nlook right.
MID_BD11_12_m01_003: Even her retinue are keeping their distance. I have a\nbad feeling about this.
MID_BD11_12_m01_004: Step back, boy. I have never seen Her Majesty so\nout of sorts.
MID_BD11_12_m01_005: I don't think we can talk her down this time. Better\nrun if you don't wanna die!
MID_BD11_12_m01_006: First Leda, now Theodora. Why did they let it get\nthis far?
MID_BD11_12_m01_007: You're too good for this! Snap out of it!
MID_BD11_12_m02: <TH>
MID_BD11_12_m02_001: Are you really sticking your neck out for the boss?
MID_BD11_12_m05: <TH>
MID_BD11_12_m02_002: I owe you one, kid! Tell me what you need to help\nstop the boss.
MID_BD11_12_m04: <TH>
MID_BD11_12_m04_004: But...the long-held dream of Saramis...
MID_BD11_12_m04_001: Is it really over now?
MID_BD11_12_m04_002: My lady! Thank heavens you were not\nmortally wounded.
MID_BD11_12_m04_003: Way to go, kid! I won't forget what you did for us\ntoday, not ever.
MID_BD11_12_e01: <TH>
MID_BD11_12_e01_001: The match is over!
MID_BD11_12_e01_002: A heart-pounding contest. And who is left standing?
MID_BD11_12_e02: <TH>
MID_BD11_12_e01_003: Ribeira Winds!
MID_BD11_12_e01_004: Shower all these warriors, who fought so valiantly,\nwith praise and admiration!
MID_SC11_13_m01: <TH>
MID_SC11_13_m01_001: Show me what you got, boys! If we make it outta\nhere, we'll be livin' the good life!
MID_SC11_13_m09: <TH>
MID_SC11_13_m01_002: Gotcha, big brother! Watch me go on a once-in-a-\nlifetime rampage!
MID_SC11_13_m02: <TH>
MID_SC11_13_m02_001: I'd heard there was a vulkan locked up in the prison.\nThat does explain your skills.
MID_SC11_13_m02_002: That...is a long story. Right now, I'm just another\ncondemned man.
MID_SC11_13_m02_003: You must have been through a lot.
MID_SC11_13_m02_004: Sure. But I've got no regrets. I've had more than my\nfair share of happiness.
MID_SC11_13_m03: <TH>
MID_SC11_13_m03_001: You sure got some interesting techniques there.
MID_SC11_13_m03_002: Reminds me of the style passed down through the\nBrezarant royal line.
MID_SC11_13_m03_003: It's been passed down in my family for generations.\nSince Brunhild, the house's founder.
MID_SC11_13_m03_004: Seems like you've been through a lot too.
MID_SC11_13_m03_005: You'll have to tell me all about it after we clean up\nthis mess.
MID_SC11_13_m04: <TH>
MID_SC11_13_m04_001: Is Cai your son? He's going to be a great\nwarrior someday.
MID_SC11_13_m04_002: He will, won't he? Castor and I are very proud of\nour Cai.
MID_SC11_13_m04_003: It is strange, someone who looks so young having a\nchild Cai's age.
MID_SC11_13_m04_004: Careful now...
MID_SC11_13_m05: <TH>
MID_SC11_13_m05_001: All we gotta do is beat you. Then the treasure's ours.
MID_SC11_13_m06: <TH>
MID_SC11_13_m06_001: That woman didn't say we'd be pursued so soon.
MID_SC11_13_m06_002: Did she set us up?
MID_SC11_13_m07: <TH>
MID_SC11_13_m07_001: Any fool who fears not death, come forward and\nface your destiny!
MID_SC11_13_m07_002: Heehee. I've always wanted to say something\nlike that.
MID_SC11_13_m08: <TH>
MID_SC11_13_m08_001: Castor! Look! I'm fighting!
MID_SC11_13_m08_002: Yeah, I can see that. How 'bout you keep your eyes\non your enemy?
MID_SC11_13_e01: <TH>
MID_SC11_13_e01_001: There's magic flowing through {SetColor=Gold}that area{SetColor=Default}. Standing on\nit will {SetColor=Gold}make you more powerful{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SC11_13_e01_002: So keep the enemy off that space! Fight smart and\nuse the magic areas to our advantage!
MID_SC11_13_e03: <TH>
MID_SC11_13_e03_001: Bwahaha! Finally caught up to you!
MID_SC11_13_e03_002: Here I was takin' a nap, and you're out here having\nall the fun!
MID_SC11_13_e03_003: Alright—c'mon, Brother. And you too, Cai!\nLet's flatten these guys!
MID_SC11_13_e02: <TH>
MID_SC11_13_e02_001: There is magic flowing into {SetColor=Gold}the floor there{SetColor=Default}. I suspect\nif we stand on it, we'll {SetColor=Gold}fight better{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC11_13_e02_002: We'll have to watch out for enemies standing on it\nand try to use them to our advantage instead.
MID_SC11_14_m01: <TH>
MID_SC11_14_m01_001: Sorry, Bertrand. This is as far as I go. My boy...\nHe's so strong.
MID_SC11_14_m01_002: Castor—your hopes. Your ambitions. They were not\nin vain.
MID_SC11_14_m02: <TH>
MID_SC11_14_m02_001: Why are you doing this, old man? Answer me!
MID_SC11_14_m02_002: Do you even care about Mom and me?
MID_SC11_14_m02_003: Enough talking. Why don't you try coming at me,\nwith everything you've got?
MID_SC11_14_m03: <TH>
MID_SC11_14_m03_001: I've got nothing against any of you. But I'm not\nholding back.
MID_SC11_14_m04: <TH>
MID_SC11_14_m04_001: Alright, Cai.
MID_SC11_14_m04_002: You really think you've progressed as a warrior?\nTime to prove it.
MID_SC11_14_m04_003: I know how this goes, Bertrand, and I'm gonna give\nyou everything I've got.
MID_SC11_14_m05: <TH>
MID_SC11_14_m05_001: I'm sorry. I have my own wish to fulfill.
MID_SC11_14_m06: <TH>
MID_SC11_14_m06_001: Bwahaha! Look at us! Look at YOU! Back at it again!\nFate's a funny thing, huh?
MID_SC11_14_m06_002: You made it so far. You're gonna lose—but ya can go\nhome with your head held high!
MID_SC11_14_m07: <TH>
MID_SC11_14_m07_001: Magnificent. I'll admit it, Cai. You win the day.
MID_SC11_14_e02: <TH>
MID_SC11_14_e02_001: You said you weren't going to show me any mercy,\nhuh? Bring it on, Dad!
MID_SC11_14_e04: <TH>
MID_SC11_14_e04_001: Now no one can interfere. OK, Cai. Show me what\nyou've learned!
MID_SC11_14_e15: <TH>
MID_SC11_14_e15_001: Those {SetColor=Gold}levers{SetColor=Default} seem to operate the magical barrier.\nIf we can {SetColor=Gold}activate them again, will it vanish{SetColor=Default}?
MID_SC11_14_e16: <TH>
MID_SC11_14_e16_001: Cai! The {SetColor=Gold}magical tiles{SetColor=Default} near you don't have much\npower, but you can {SetColor=Gold}still use them {SetColor=Default}if you're in trouble!
MID_SC11_14_e11: <TH>
MID_SC11_14_e11_001: <DLG>Effects of used magical spots have ended.
MID_SC11_14_e14: <TH>
MID_SC11_14_e14_001: The wall's gone?! Whew, now I can move!
MID_SC11_XX_Rewind_e01: <TH>
MID_SC11_XX_Rewind_e01_001: Huh?! That bag of sand... It's glowing!